{"id": "tea:mumuksuppadi:1", "source": "src:mumuksuppadi", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "The tirumantra: 'oṃ' shows the soul to be the Lord's alone (ananyārha-śeṣatva); 'namaḥ' removes the sense of belonging to oneself and of being one's own means; 'nārāyaṇāya' is the prayer for service to Nārāyaṇa in all states.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "terms": ["trm:tirumantra", "trm:ananyarha-sesatva"], "concepts": ["cpt:rahasya-traya", "cpt:sesa-sesi-bhava"], "practices": ["prc:tirumantra-japa"], "teachers": ["tch:pillai-lokacarya"], "speaker": "Piḷḷai Lokācārya", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U14-visistadvaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U14-visistadvaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:mumuksuppadi:2", "source": "src:mumuksuppadi", "location": {"ref": "2"}, "paraphrase": "The dvaya: the first half shows Śrī as mediator (puruṣakāra) and the Lord's feet, with his qualities of motherly love (vātsalya), lordship (svāmitva), gracious condescension (sauśīlya) and accessibility (saulabhya), as the means; the second half is the prayer for service to the divine couple, removing any sense that the service is for oneself.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "practice"], "terms": ["trm:dvaya-mantra", "trm:purusakara", "trm:vatsalya", "trm:svamitva", "trm:sausilya", "trm:saulabhya"], "concepts": ["cpt:rahasya-traya", "cpt:purusakara"], "practices": ["prc:dvaya-anusandhana"], "teachers": ["tch:pillai-lokacarya"], "speaker": "Piḷḷai Lokācārya", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U14-visistadvaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U14-visistadvaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:mumuksuppadi:3", "source": "src:mumuksuppadi", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "The carama-śloka: 'abandoning all dharmas' means giving up every other means, including the idea that one's own surrender is a means; 'me alone' means the Lord himself, already accomplished, is the only means; 'do not grieve' — all burden is his.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:carama-sloka", "trm:siddhopaya"], "concepts": ["cpt:siddhopaya-sadhyopaya", "cpt:prapatti"], "cross_refs": ["tea:bhagavad-gita:18.66"], "disputes": ["dsp:is-prapatti-an-upaya"], "teachers": ["tch:pillai-lokacarya"], "speaker": "Piḷḷai Lokācārya", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U14-visistadvaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U14-visistadvaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
